# QA replay of the stash desk's view (owner, 2026-10-19, from a panel: A1 · B1 · C1 · D2, and the addendum: A(2) · B1 ·
# C1a · Da; step B part 2, the view): the made-up desk (Rules.DeskExample) as readings in the menus bring it. The desk
# takes the map's place by itself, its page comes in cell by cell and its totals count up; a window's cell and head
# light each other; a cell's card stands in the rail; a reading that changed the backpack folds the rest, a name opens
# its region, a reading that changed nothing changes nothing; PLAN and DESK switch; a raid takes the window and gives it
# back to Plan, the desk keeping its page. A developer build plays it with --dev-view --dev-script; how to run it, and
# what each still must show: desk.md beside this file. Times are in seconds.

# A --dev-view session starts on settings of its own, as at a first start, so the tour opened by itself at chapter 1
# once the data was there. It ends first.
tour end
map customs
wait 3

# The first reading: every region opens, its cells coming in 50 ms apart, the head line counting up.
desk 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\entry
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\first

# The Zhuk's cell in the backpack: its window's head and the stem light up; the rail says "One of 2 items".
desk point backpack 0 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\window

# The LEDX in the stash: its item card in the rail.
desk point stash 8 0
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\card

# A reading that changed the backpack (a LEDX more): the backpack opens and comes in, the rest folds.
desk 2
wait 3
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\fold
# STASH's name in its fold line clicked: the stash opens, until the next reading.
desk open stash
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\unfold
# The same page again: a reading that changed nothing changes nothing.
desk 3
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\same

# PLAN, then DESK: the map back, then the page as it was.
desk plan
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\plan
desk show
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\show

# A raid loading takes the window, with no click; when it is over, Plan, and DESK shows the page kept. The stills after
# the raid wait out the RAID OVER cue (a still taken while a cue fades fails to render it).
load
steps
wait 2
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\raid
start
wait 2
end
wait 7
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\after
desk show
wait 1
snapshot %TEMP%\shturmap-qa\desk\kept
exit
